<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Japan gives Benin another $14 million for schools.</title>
<headline>Japan gives Benin another $14 million for schools.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Japan has given Benin around eight billion CFA francs ($14 million) to build 65 schools, the Japanese embassy in Ivory Coast said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>This is the second phase of a programme that will eventually give Benin a total of 89 new schools, with 354 classrooms, for a total cost of over 11 billion CFA francs. ($ = 580 CFA francs)</p>
</text>
